What this dataset does and does not contain
---------------------------------------------
Each record in `data/scenarios/scenarios.jsonl` contains:

1. Originally-authored generic content (`scenario.preconditions`,
   `scenario.process`, `scenario.impact`, `scenario.remediation`) drawn from
   `knowledge/vulnerability_playbooks.json` -- written for this project, not
   copied from any specific writeup. This content is CC BY 4.0 by this
   project.

2. Factual classification metadata about a real, publicly disclosed report or
   writeup (title, vulnerability class, severity, program name, author name,
   disclosure date, a source URL). This metadata is derived from information
   the source platforms (HackerOne's public Hacktivity, Pentester Land's
   public writeup index, public GitHub repositories) already make available
   for exactly this kind of reuse.

3. A link (`source.url`) back to the original writeup.

This dataset intentionally does NOT reproduce the body text of any bug bounty
report or blog writeup. If you want the full narrative, follow `source.url`
to the original, which remains under whatever license/copyright its own
author has applied to it -- that is unaffected by this project's license.

If you are a source author and want your writeup's metadata removed from this
dataset, please open an issue with the `source.url` in question.
